### 1. Use Adobe Premiere Pro's Built-in Features
Adobe Premiere Pro offers several built-in features that can help you automate repetitive tasks:

- **Batch Processing**: Use the Batch command to apply the same effects or settings to multiple clips.
- **Dynamic Link**: Seamlessly transfer projects between Adobe Premiere Pro and After Effects for complex animations and effects.
- **Source Monitor**: Quickly preview and trim clips before importing them into your project.

### 2. Utilize Automation Scripts
While Adobe Premiere Pro does not natively support Python scripting, you can use JavaScript (jsx) to automate tasks. Here's an example of how you might write a simple script to import clips and apply basic settings:

```javascript
// Import necessary modules
var app = Premiere.app;
var proj = app.project;

// Define the input and output folders
var inputFolder = "C:/path/to/input_clips";
var outputFolder = "C:/path/to/output_clips";

// Function to import clips and apply settings
function importAndProcessClips(folderPath) {
    var folder = new Folder(folderPath);
    var files = folder.getFiles();

    for (var i = 0; i < files.length; i++) {
        var file = files[i];
        var clipItem = proj.importFile(file.fsName);

        // Apply basic settings (example: set duration to 10 seconds)
